ing on which computer (the server or the client) executes them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="32556">client-side</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1789527">bezeroaren aldeko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10561_19019_2085144"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A task that is part of an operating system or program, and is operating without interaction with the user while the user is working on another task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="19019">background task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085144">atzeko planoko zeregin</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10565_375737_380181"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The practice of deploying new Edge Transport servers based on the configuration information of a previously configured source server. The configuration information of the previously configured source server is copied and exported to an XML file, which is then imported to the target server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="375737">cloned configuration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml