e information for easy retrieval and sorting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748513">Categories</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228316">Etiketak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20861_748513_1228317"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows the user to apply custom or default markers to items (e.g. Outlook messages or OneNote content) in order to categorize information for easy retrieval and sorting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748513">Categories</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228317">Kategoriak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20863_748907_2330890"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual depiction of a weighted list. The cloud contains keywords or tags associated with a text or Web site, and formatting (e.g. color and/or size) is used to indicate the relative importance of each item, or frequency with which it occurs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748907">tag cloud</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2330890">etiketa-hodei</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20865_748916_2084619"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature in Internet Explorer that helps detect phishing websites and can help protect you from installing malicious software or malware.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748916">SmartScreen Filter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084619">SmartScreen iragazkia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20867_2676671_2677429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows the user to fill cells with data that follows a pattern or that is based on data in other cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2676671">AutoFill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2677429">Betetze automatikoa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20867_752822_2677429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows the user to fill cells with data that follows a pattern or that is based on data in other cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="752822">Auto Fill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2677429">Betetze automatikoa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20869_756841_1168756"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An Internet Explorer feature where the domain of the site you are visiting is darker and the rest of the URL is lighter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="756841">domain highlighting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1168756">Nabarmendu domeinua</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2087_22056_1137298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A page where there is no information displayed</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="22056">blank page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1137298">orri huts</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20872_757060_1168752"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of browser extension that gives users quick access to their Web and client applications from any Web page. An Accelerator can run on user-selected data, links, and the current document. This browser extension can provide “lookup” service like in-place definition or “send” service like sending selected text to a Web email provider.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="757060">Accelerator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1168752">bizkortzailea</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20873_757096_1168754"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Browsing or navigating through a page using the arrow keys, PAGE UP, PAGE DOWN, HOME and END keys.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="757096">Caret Browsing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1168754">Teklatu bidezko arakatzea</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20883_759067_1355390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of creating and sending text messages between or to mobile phones and devices using the SMS protocol.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759067">text messaging</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1355390">testu-mezularitza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20884_759071_1228318"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any hardware or software that can detect events or environmental changes, such as your current location or the amount of light around your computer. For example, a notebook with a location sensor, such as a Global Positioning System (GPS) receiver, can determine your exact location. An ambient light sensor can detect when there is a change in lighting, and then a program can use that information to adjust the brightness of your screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759071">sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228318">sentsore</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20888_759108_1228319"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that includes an antenna, a radio receiver, and a processor for use with the worldwide GPS (Global Positioning System). A GPS receiver uses position and time information from four GPS satellites to calculate precise information about its current location, its speed of travel, and the current time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759108">GPS receiver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228319">GPS hargailu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20889_759109_1228320"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that can detect the current location of your computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759109">location sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228320">kokaleku-sentsore</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20894_759503_1228321"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Technologies that measure and analyze physical and behavioral human characteristics, such as fingerprints, eye retinas and irises, voice patterns, facial patterns, hand measurements, typing patterns and signatures, to recognize or authenticate identity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759503">biometrics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228321">biometria</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20896_759507_1359763"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A library of controls that support user interface development. Some of these controls function as containers for other controls or content, such as images and media.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759507">Control Gallery</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1359763">Kontrol-galeria</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="209_40581_2802068"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A binary file that a programmer can load into a debugger to analyze the cause of the crash. It contains the contents of the memory when the crash occurred.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="40581">crash dump</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2802068">memoria-iraulketa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="209_640753_2802068"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A binary file that a programmer can load into a debugger to analyze the cause of the crash. It contains the contents of the memory when the crash occurred.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="640753">dump</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNo