s termination by the process itself or by another application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766809">silent process exit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228347">prozesu-irteera isil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21114_766811_1228348"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To shut down a core processor for power saving purpose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766811">park</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228348">desaktibatu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21115_766812_1228349"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reopen a core processor that had been parked for power saving purpose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766812">unpark</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228349">aktibatu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21116_766813_1228350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Windows Media Player that allows users to remove gaps between tracks that they burn to audio CDs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766813">gapless CD burning</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228350">tarterik gabeko grabatzea</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21116_766816_1228350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Windows Media Player that allows users to remove gaps between tracks that they burn to audio CDs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766816">gapless burning</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228350">tarterik gabeko grabatzea</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21117_766814_1228351"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Existing in reference to the removal of silences or clicks between tracks when they are burnt to an audio CD or when they are played back from the CD.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766814">gapless</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1228351">tar