 medium. The floppy disk used today is the rigid 3.5-inch microfloppy that holds 1.44 MB. It is called floppy because the first varieties were housed in bendable jackets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="339962">disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="441007">disko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24903_1165764_3138419"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option that isolates the foreground portion of an image and make the background transparent.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165764">Remove Background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3138419">Kendu atzealdea</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24913_1165825_1789667"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lets users receive and send mail from other email accounts in Outlook Web App. They can add and delete those accounts, check their account synchronization status, and manage email from those accounts in their Inbox using Inbox rules.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165825">Connected Accounts</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml: