stment function of the Kinect sensor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991457">auto-tilt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2917405">inklinazio automatiko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34348_1991458_2917918"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The infrared camera component of the Kinect sensor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991458">depth sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2917918">sakonera-sentsore</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34349_1991459_2920649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The RGB camera component of the Kinect sensor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991459">video sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2920649">bideo-sentsore</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34350_1991460_2917970"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The entire area that the sensor can "see," including walls, furniture, and other obstructions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991460">field of view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2917970">ikuseremu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34351_1991461_2543557"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The area within the Kinect sensor's field of view is able to detect a person or in which a player moves.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991461">play space</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2543557">jolas-eremua</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34352_1991462_2917957"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Facial identification used by the sensor to recognize a player.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991462">facial recognition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2917957">aurpegi-ezagutza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34353_1991463_2918028"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A motion made by a player that's intended to be tracked by the sensor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991463">gesture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918028">keinu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34354_1991464_2918030"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In-game gesture that invokes the Kinect Guide.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991464">guide gesture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918030">gidaren keinu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34355_1991465_2918098"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Biometric recognition of a player by the system, through the use of the Kinect sensor and software.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991465">Kinect ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918098">Kinect IDa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34356_1991466_2918033"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The visual progress indicator that appears in the corner of the screen when a player performs the guide gesture. Because the icon is only visible when cued by the guide gesture, use only when necessary to specifically call out its functionality, as in an instructional demo, for example.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991466">guide icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918033">gidaren ikono</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34357_1991467_2918036"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The icon that appears when a player is detected in the play space, prompting a wave to engage with Kinect. Once engaged, a hand pointer appears, which serves as a mechanism for navigation and object manipulation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991467">hand icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2918036">eskuaren ikono</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34358_1991468_2920140"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The icon that is present when the Kinect microphone is available to accept voice commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991468">microphone icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2920140">mikrofonoaren ikono</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34359_1991469_2920498"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Spoken input that's intended to be received and interpreted by the sensor as input.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991469">speech</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2920498">ahots</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="34360_1991470_2920630"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The detection and following of a person's movements by the sensor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1991470">tracking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2920630">jarraipen</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntr