es from the on-premise instance of SQL Server and generates a self-signed SSL certificate as part of its first run to run as a Local System account, a configuration file to configure itself, and a Windows Firewall rule to allow its incoming TCP connections at default port 11435.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2304644">Cloud Adapter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2307499">Hodeiko moldagailu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="39497_2304645_2307500"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An authentication mechanism that allows a security token service (STS) in one trust domain to delegate user authentication to an identity provider in another trust domain, while generating a security token for the user, when there is a trust relationship between the two domains.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2304645">federated authentication</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2307500">autentifikazio federatu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="39497_2361909_2307500"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An authentication mechanism that allows a security token service (STS) in one trust domain to delegate user authentication to an identity provider in 