 implies that the recipient is not required to take any action; the message is for informational purposes only. In a cc directive, the fact that this recipient received the mail is printed in the mail header and is thus known to all other recipients.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27858">courtesy copy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="439338">cc</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5719_27858_439339"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A directive to an email program to send a complete copy of a given piece of mail to another individual. The use of cc mail addressing, as opposed to directly addressing the mail to a person, generally implies that the recipient is not required to take any action; the message is for informational purposes only. In a cc directive, the fact that this recipient received the mail is printed in the mail header and is thus known to all other recipients.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27858">courtesy copy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="439339">kortesiako kopia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5725_295557_440677"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a process that is performed by a person, rather than automated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="295557">manual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="440677">eskuzko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5726_269749_440641"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A state in which users fill out forms when working offline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269749">offline mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="440641">lineaz kanpoko modu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5728_25995_439318"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that enables a broadband connection to the Internet by using cable television infrastructure. Access speeds vary greatly, with a maximum throughput of 10 megabits per second (Mbps).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25995">cable modem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="439318">kable-modem</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="573_231958_440372"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of coordinates that a cell occupies on a worksheet. For example, the reference of the cell that appears at the intersection of column B and row 3 is B3.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231958">cell reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="440372">gelaxka-erreferentzia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5731_155920_1664760"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of preventing a denial of service attack by limiting the number of requests that can be made to a system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="155920">throttling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1664760">eskaera-mugapen</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5731_1645777_1664760"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of preventing a denial of service attack by limiting the number of requests that can be made to a system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1645777">request throttling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1664760">eskaera-mugapen</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5738_44359_439465"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To eliminate text, a file, or part of a document with the intention of removing the information permanently.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44359">delete</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="439465">ezabatu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5754_228518_440364"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The difference between two values, such as the difference between estimated and actual expenses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228518">variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="440364">bariantza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5759_235060_440461"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Control Panel item that allows the user to view saved networks and reconnect to them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235060">Saved networks</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="440461">Gordetako sareak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5761_7364_1789475"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A phone number that subscribers can dial to reach online services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7364">access number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1789475">atzipen-zenbaki</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5766_1606_1137330"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A 16-byte value generated from the unique identifier on a device, the current date and time, and a sequence number that is used to identify a particular device, component, user, or session.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1606">globally-unique identifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1137330">identifikatzaile esklusibo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry i