 with .dll extensions. These routines are loaded only when needed by the program that calls them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="47296">DLL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="427751">Dynamic-link Library (esteka dinamikoko liburutegi)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="719_47296_427752"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An operating system feature that allows executable routines (generally serving a specific function or set of functions) to be stored separately as files with .dll extensions. These routines are loaded only when needed by the program that calls them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="47296">DLL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="eu"><ntig><termGrp><term id="427752">DLL</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="719_47297_427751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An operating system feature that allows executable routines (generally serving a specific function or set of functions) to be stored separately as files with .dll extensions. These routines are loaded only when needed by the program that calls them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="47297">dynamic-link library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNu